01:04:31,279 --> 01:04:32,843
That is a promise.

1091
01:04:36,805 --> 01:04:41,532
Alcohol and sleeping pills, death of a depressed man.

1092
01:04:41,636 --> 01:04:43,965
What a waste.

1093
01:04:44,070 --> 01:04:45,911
What a waste.

1094
01:04:46,016 --> 01:04:48,588
What the hell happened here Ben?

1095
01:04:48,692 --> 01:04:52,689
Look, sir, this was my case.

1096
01:04:52,793 --> 01:04:53,906
You gave it to me.

1097
01:04:54,010 --> 01:04:56,409
I promised you a result and I blew it.

1098
01:04:56,512 --> 01:04:58,041
You can have my resignation.

1099
01:04:58,146 --> 01:04:59,918
Ben, no.

1100
01:05:00,023 --> 01:05:01,551
This was down to me.

1101
01:05:01,657 --> 01:05:03,151
I won't let them crucify you because I

1102
01:05:03,255 --> 01:05:06,141
didn't cover all the angles.

1103
01:05:06,245 --> 01:05:07,148
I want to take the play.

1104
01:05:07,253 --> 01:05:08,469
No, Ben, no.

1105
01:05:08,572 --> 01:05:09,477
You can just stop that.

1106
01:05:09,581 --> 01:05:10,728
You can forget all about it.

1107
01:05:10,832 --> 01:05:13,022
I won't accept your resignation.

1108
01:05:13,127 --> 01:05:14,516
Dear God, Ben, sometimes I think you're

1109
01:05:14,620 --> 01:05:15,977
the only one that I can trust.

1110
01:05:18,167 --> 01:05:19,209
Thank you, sir.

1111
01:05:29,289 --> 01:05:30,957
I'm really sorry about yesterday.

1112
01:05:31,061 --> 01:05:34,050
I think he was just under a lot of pressure, you know?

1113
01:05:34,154 --> 01:05:37,039
So long as you're all right.

1114
01:05:37,144 --> 01:05:41,453
And anyway, it's my birthday today.

1115
01:05:41,557 --> 01:05:43,192
Though you could help me celebrate.

1116
01:05:43,296 --> 01:05:45,207
Drinking on duty, are we?

1117
01:05:45,312 --> 01:05:48,579
Well, I won't tell anyone if you don't.

1118
01:05:48,683 --> 01:05:50,455
We could get something to eat.

1119
01:05:50,559 --> 01:05:53,341
Yeah, good idea.

1120
01:05:53,445 --> 01:05:54,591
Oh, hey.

1121
01:05:54,695 --> 01:05:56,121
Get some glasses.

1122
01:05:56,225 --> 01:05:59,319
I think a birthday deserves a bit of fizz, don't you?

1123
01:05:59,423 --> 01:06:00,604
Yeah, why not?

1124
01:06:00,709 --> 01:06:01,578
Oh!

1125
01:06:09,364 --> 01:06:10,648
- Well, cheers. - Cheers.

1126
01:06:10,753 --> 01:06:11,587
Happy birthday.

1127
01:06:18,956 --> 01:06:21,286
Mike.

1128
01:06:21,390 --> 01:06:22,744
It's not on, OK?

1129
01:06:26,081 --> 01:06:27,784
You sure about that?

1130
01:06:27,888 --> 01:06:29,695
Yeah, absolutely.

1131
01:06:29,800 --> 01:06:33,588
Honestly, for all sorts of reasons.

1132
01:06:33,692 --> 01:06:34,945
Let's not spoil things.

1133
01:06:38,559 --> 01:06:40,332
OK.

1134
01:06:40,437 --> 01:06:41,305
Sorry.

1135
01:06:41,410 --> 01:06:43,112
Friends, OK?

1136
01:06:43,217 --> 01:06:44,085
Friends.

1137
01:06:47,874 --> 01:06:50,376
Is it all right if I still fancy you?

1138
01:06:50,482 --> 01:06:52,983
So long as you know it's not going to come to anything.

1139
01:06:53,087 --> 01:06:55,277
I would much rather you didn't though.

1140
01:06:55,382 --> 01:06:57,675
There's no hope of that.

1141
01:06:57,780 --> 01:06:58,753
Right.

1142
01:06:58,857 --> 01:07:01,360
What are we having?

1143
01:07:01,464 --> 01:07:03,967
The case against the three policemen accused

1144
01:07:04,071 --> 01:07:06,608
of manslaughter in the Billy Coats trial

1145
01:07:06,712 --> 01:07:10,049
collapsed amid dramatic scenes at the Old Bailey this morning.

1146
01:07:10,153 --> 01:07:14,046
Well, sir, in confidence, we were told to push too hard.

1147
01:07:14,150 --> 01:07:15,923
He was so keen to get a result, the boy

1148
01:07:16,027 --> 01:07:18,357
put a spin on his story to show willing, then

1149
01:07:18,461 --> 01:07:21,727
panicked when it came to the push.

1150
01:07:21,831 --> 01:07:22,805
That's a shame.

1151
01:07:22,909 --> 01:07:26,106
Is John Othello all right, Ben?

1152
01:07:26,211 --> 01:07:27,601
Is there anything we should know about?

1153
01:07:27,705 --> 01:07:30,729
He's under a lot of stress, put it that way.

1154
01:07:30,833 --> 01:07:32,850
Let's say, we're looking after him the best way we can.

1155
01:07:42,825 --> 01:07:44,076
I'm having a lovely time, are you

1156
01:07:44,180 --> 01:07:46,092
Well, not quite as lovely as I thought.

1157
01:07:46,196 --> 01:07:47,934
[laughing]

1158
01:07:48,039 --> 01:07:49,011
No, not bad.

1159
01:07:49,116 --> 01:07:50,054
Not bad.

1160
01:07:50,158 --> 01:07:52,174
Time for a proper drink though.

1161
01:07:52,278 --> 01:07:54,364
That champagne is just girls' wine really.

1162
01:07:54,469 --> 01:07:55,789
Excellent.

1163
01:07:55,894 --> 01:07:57,596
They don't muck about down there in the Cote-Rotie.

1164
01:07:57,701 --> 01:07:59,716
Would you care to taste this wine, sir.

1165
01:07:59,821 --> 01:08:01,802
All right, partner, I don't mind if I do.

1166
01:08:01,906 --> 01:08:02,983
Put it in there.

1167
01:08:06,772 --> 01:08:07,641
Take it off.

1168
01:08:07,746 --> 01:08:09,345
I'll soak it.

1169
01:08:09,449 --> 01:08:10,318
You sure?

1170
01:08:10,422 --> 01:08:11,742
You can borrow something of John's.

1171
01:08:23,803 --> 01:08:26,201
[water runs]

1172
01:08:26,305 --> 01:08:28,912
I should think you're about the same size, aren't you?

1173
01:08:34,022 --> 01:08:34,891
What about this.

1174
01:08:34,995 --> 01:08:36,107
No, not that.

1175
01:08:36,212 --> 01:08:37,324
Take it off please.

1176
01:08:37,429 --> 01:08:38,679
Hey, why doesn't it suit me?

1177
01:08:46,082 --> 01:08:48,202
Sir.

1178
01:08:48,308 --> 01:08:50,219
Michael spilled some wine on his shirt

1179
01:08:50,323 --> 01:08:52,373
and I just went to give him something else to wear

1180
01:08:52,479 --> 01:08:53,625
and he found that.

1181
01:08:53,729 --> 01:08:56,231
[snickers]

1182
01:08:57,796 --> 01:08:58,699
Take it off.

1183
01:09:03,288 --> 01:09:05,615
Look, I was just going to anyway, sir.

1184
01:09:08,258 --> 01:09:09,335
It's my birthday, sir.

1185
01:09:09,439 --> 01:09:13,297
I brought a bottle of wine.

1186
01:09:13,401 --> 01:09:14,410
Right.

1187
01:09:14,513 --> 01:09:15,418
You'll be all right?

1188
01:09:15,521 --> 01:09:16,703
Fine, fine.

1189
01:09:16,807 --> 01:09:18,614
I think he's a bit upset about something.

1190
01:09:18,719 --> 01:09:19,553
OK.

1191
01:09:19,657 --> 01:09:22,439
Well, if you're sure.

1192
01:09:22,542 --> 01:09:24,350
And um, right.

1193
01:09:32,484 --> 01:09:33,908
John.

1194
01:09:34,013 --> 01:09:34,985
How was today?

1195
01:09:35,090 --> 01:09:37,591
How could you give him that to wear?

1196
01:09:37,697 --> 01:09:38,670
I told you. I didn't.

1197
01:09:38,774 --> 01:09:39,817
He just happened to pick it up.

1198
01:09:39,921 --> 01:09:41,242
He just happened to pick it up.

1199
01:09:41,346 --> 01:09:42,945
Of all the things that he could put on his body.

1200
01:09:45,899 --> 01:09:46,872
I know.

1201
01:09:46,976 --> 01:09:47,915
I'm sorry.

1202
01:09:48,019 --> 01:09:49,201
He only had it on for a second.

1203
01:09:49,306 --> 01:09:50,834
As soon as I saw it, I said, take it off

1204
01:09:50,939 --> 01:09:52,086
and then you came in.

1205
01:09:52,190 --> 01:09:53,615
Because he spilled wine on his shirt.

1206
01:09:53,720 --> 01:09:55,249
And I'm supposed to believe that?

1207
01:09:55,354 --> 01:09:56,188
It's in there.

1208
01:09:56,292 --> 01:09:59,350
It's soaking.

1209
01:09:59,455 --> 01:10:00,740
John, what is this?

1210
01:10:06,544 --> 01:10:11,654
You think I'm having an affair with Michael, don't you?

1211
01:10:11,758 --> 01:10:13,009
Are you?

1212
01:10:13,114 --> 01:10:15,478
No.

1213
01:10:15,581 --> 01:10:18,675
John, I've never looked at another man since I met you.

1214
01:10:18,779 --> 01:10:20,586
You're the love of my life.

1215
01:10:20,690 --> 01:10:24,097
I thought you knew that.

1216
01:10:24,201 --> 01:10:26,183
Yeah, well, sometimes I don't know what to believe.

1217
01:10:26,287 --> 01:10:28,408
John, with all the things you have to worry about, you

1218
01:10:28,511 --> 01:10:30,179
don't have to worry about me,

1219
01:10:30,284 --> 01:10:31,708
Truly?

1220
01:10:31,812 --> 01:10:35,810
Truly, cross my heart and hope to die.

1221
01:10:38,729 --> 01:10:40,572
Sometimes I think I love you too much.

1222
01:10:40,676 --> 01:10:42,866
Well, that's not possible.

1223
01:10:42,970 --> 01:10:45,195
I can take all the love you have to give me.

1224
01:10:45,299 --> 01:10:46,550
Oh, really?

1225
01:10:46,654 --> 01:10:47,697
Yes, really.

1226
01:10:51,312 --> 01:10:53,328
Really?

1227
01:10:53,433 --> 01:10:54,301
Really?

1228
01:11:02,051 --> 01:11:03,164
Put me down.

1229
01:11:10,706 --> 01:11:13,313
I can't get away, can I?

1230
01:11:13,417 --> 01:11:15,816
I'll never let you go.

1231
01:11:15,920 --> 01:11:18,492
Never going to let you go.

1232
01:11:18,596 --> 01:11:21,168
[typing sounds]

1233
01:11:23,775 --> 01:11:26,173
JOHN OTHELLO: I don't know, Ben.

1234
01:11:26,278 --> 01:11:28,293
I don't know.

1235
01:11:28,397 --> 01:11:33,194
This robe, do you still have it?

1236
01:11:33,298 --> 01:11:35,801
Yes.

1237
01:11:35,905 --> 01:11:37,712
Good.

1238
01:11:37,817 --> 01:11:39,902
Let me have the lab take a look at it.

1239
01:11:40,006 --> 01:11:42,578
What for?

1240
01:11:42,682 --> 01:11:45,567
You know what for, John.

1241
01:11:45,672 --> 01:11:48,453
Sexual secretions.

1242
01:11:48,556 --> 01:11:52,657
Yours, his, hers.

1243
01:11:52,761 --> 01:11:55,369
I'll make sure it's confidential.

1244
01:11:55,474 --> 01:12:00,409
You're A. She's B. He's C. Look if there's anything

1245
01:12:00,512 --> 01:12:03,016
you'll know for certain.

1246
01:12:03,120 --> 01:12:06,144
Maybe we shouldn't be doing this, Ben.

1247
01:12:06,248 --> 01:12:09,758
You know, it could all just be in my head.

1248
01:12:09,863 --> 01:12:12,296
Well, if it was, that's good.

1249
01:12:12,401 --> 01:12:15,076
But if you don't find out, you'll always be wondering.

1250
01:12:18,379 --> 01:12:19,699
You do want to know, don't you, John?

1251
01:12:22,757 --> 01:12:25,017
Yes.

1252
01:12:25,121 --> 01:12:26,580
I want to know.

1253
01:12:37,252 --> 01:12:40,171
This is a beautiful gown.

1254
01:12:40,276 --> 01:12:41,526
She bought it for me.

1255
01:12:44,758 --> 01:12:45,627
She has an eye.

1256
01:12:51,535 --> 01:12:56,403
Now, they showed me how to do this.

1257
01:12:56,506 --> 01:12:58,557
Open your mouth, John.

1258
01:12:58,661 --> 01:12:59,530
Only take a second.

1259
01:13:10,305 --> 01:13:11,417
That should do it.

1260
01:13:11,521 --> 01:13:12,668
And what about him?

1261
01:13:12,773 --> 01:13:16,318
All taken care of.

1262
01:13:16,423 --> 01:13:19,515
Now, let's have a drink.

1263
01:13:22,608 --> 01:13:24,348
You want some of this?

1264
01:13:24,452 --> 01:13:25,355
Oh, Christ, Ben.

1265
01:13:25,459 --> 01:13:26,119
What is that?

1266
01:13:26,223 --> 01:13:28,170
It's not dope, is it?

1267
01:13:31,090 --> 01:13:34,564
Dundee cake, my little weakness.

1268
01:13:34,670 --> 01:13:35,955
My mum used to make it.

1269
01:13:36,060 --> 01:13:39,918
Neither of my two wives could be asked.

1270
01:13:40,022 --> 01:13:41,204
It's good.

1271
01:13:41,309 --> 01:13:42,178
Have some.

1272
01:13:42,282 --> 01:13:43,150
Go on.

1273
01:13:50,067 --> 01:13:51,700
I don't know what's happening to me, Ben.

1274
01:13:51,804 --> 01:13:55,002
Eat your cake.

1275
01:13:55,107 --> 01:13:56,358
It's good for you.

1276
01:13:56,462 --> 01:13:57,992
I mean, this you can rely on, right?

1277
01:14:02,509 --> 01:14:05,221
I know what you're talking about.

1278
01:14:05,326 --> 01:14:07,723
I feel like that sometimes.

1279
01:14:07,827 --> 01:14:09,427
One minute everything's fine.

1280
01:14:09,530 --> 01:14:10,851
Everything's under control.

1281
01:14:10,955 --> 01:14:13,181
The, next they've snatched the rug from under you.

1282
01:14:13,285 --> 01:14:17,316
You're like whirling down into some dark pit, ass over tit.

1283
01:14:17,422 --> 01:14:18,846
You don't know which way up you are.

1284
01:14:18,950 --> 01:14:20,202
You feel like that?

1285
01:14:20,306 --> 01:14:22,357
I've felt like that.

1286
01:14:22,461 --> 01:14:25,207
The thing is, don't let it show.

1287
01:14:25,311 --> 01:14:26,840
Don't let it show and it will pass.

1288
01:14:31,879 --> 01:14:34,035
Let's all go out to dinner, my treat.

1289
01:14:34,139 --> 01:14:37,962
We'll have a private room at Fernando's.

1290
01:14:38,066 --> 01:14:39,873
I don't think I could handle it, Ben.

1291
01:14:39,977 --> 01:14:42,273
You can handle it.

1292
01:14:42,377 --> 01:14:44,254
Show them who's master of the situation.

1293
01:14:48,737 --> 01:14:50,440
You know, you're right.

1294
01:14:55,480 --> 01:14:58,470
[laughing]

1295
01:14:58,573 --> 01:15:00,971
God, this stuff is great.

1296
01:15:01,075 --> 01:15:02,258
Everybody, drink up.

1297
01:15:05,351 --> 01:15:09,765
John, I always meant to ask you, what's your history?

1298
01:15:09,869 --> 01:15:11,885
I mean, where does your family come from originally,

1299
01:15:11,989 --> 01:15:13,587
if you don't mind my asking.

1300
01:15:13,692 --> 01:15:15,291
I don't mind you asking me, Lulu.

1301
01:15:15,396 --> 01:15:16,716
My father's from St. Lucia.

1302
01:15:16,820 --> 01:15:17,967
That's where my people are from.

1303
01:15:18,071 --> 01:15:20,713
And before that of course, West Africa.

1304
01:15:20,817 --> 01:15:24,432
St. Lucia was just absolutely beautiful,

1305
01:15:24,536 --> 01:15:27,733
rain forest stretching right down to the ocean.

1306
01:15:27,838 --> 01:15:30,376
It's paradise really, wasn't it?

1307
01:15:30,480 --> 01:15:33,191
Blacks waiting on whites, just like they did in the old days

1308
01:15:33,295 --> 01:15:35,103
on the plantations.

1309
01:15:35,207 --> 01:15:37,328
You get a very good sense of what it must have been like.

1310
01:15:37,432 --> 01:15:38,475
You see, Lulu.

1311
01:15:38,578 --> 01:15:40,732
That's what St. Lucia's all about.

1312
01:15:40,838 --> 01:15:43,375
St. Lucia, Grenada, Barbados, all of those places.

1313
01:15:43,479 --> 01:15:47,059
Your people brought my people over there to work and die

1314
01:15:47,163 --> 01:15:49,979
as slaves on your plantations.

1315
01:15:52,620 --> 01:15:54,288
There was an old man, what was his name?

1316
01:15:57,625 --> 01:15:58,876
Joshua.

1317
01:15:58,981 --> 01:16:00,822
He was a Gardener in the hotel.

1318
01:16:00,926 --> 01:16:02,492
His grandmother knew my grandmother.

1319
01:16:02,595 --> 01:16:05,619
He could show you every inch of the island

1320
01:16:05,723 --> 01:16:08,296
and tell you what happened.

1321
01:16:08,400 --> 01:16:13,092
And he showed me where my family worked and died.

1322
01:16:16,741 --> 01:16:17,923
I can't explain that to you.

1323
01:16:18,028 --> 01:16:19,905
I don't really expect you to understand.

1324
01:16:20,009 --> 01:16:21,712
I think we do, John.

1325
01:16:21,816 --> 01:16:24,458
Well, it's all supposed to be different now, isn't it?

1326
01:16:24,561 --> 01:16:27,308
I mean, my people came over here, start a new life

1327
01:16:27,412 --> 01:16:29,949
and what did they get?

1328
01:16:30,054 --> 01:16:34,120
The leftovers of the men's leavings.

1329
01:16:39,994 --> 01:16:42,983
You haven't done too badly.

1330
01:16:43,087 --> 01:16:44,200
Haven't I?

1331
01:16:48,266 --> 01:16:50,004
You've never said anything like that before.

1332
01:16:50,108 --> 01:16:51,325
Maybe I was too ashamed.

1333
01:16:51,429 --> 01:16:52,853
Ashamed of what?

1334
01:16:52,958 --> 01:16:54,175
Ashamed that the part of me that when I was younger,

1335
01:16:54,279 --> 01:16:57,199
wanted to be like you, wanted to be white.

1336
01:16:59,700 --> 01:17:01,231
I mean, who the hell wants to be the nigger?

1337
01:17:07,243 --> 01:17:08,772
What is he doing here?

1338
01:17:08,876 --> 01:17:09,745
I asked him to come.

1339
01:17:09,850 --> 01:17:10,788
Please don't be angry.

1340
01:17:10,893 --> 01:17:12,596
He just wants to talk to you.

1341
01:17:12,700 --> 01:17:15,273
What is that man doing here?

1342
01:17:15,377 --> 01:17:17,531
All right, John, look, this isn't a good idea.

1343
01:17:17,636 --> 01:17:19,755
Sir, I need to speak to you.

1344
01:17:19,860 --> 01:17:21,875
You've got the wrong idea about me.

1345
01:17:21,981 --> 01:17:23,682
How dare you come here and speak to me.

1346
01:17:23,788 --> 01:17:26,082
Someone's been spreading lies, sir.

1347
01:17:26,186 --> 01:17:27,437
Something's going on.

1348
01:17:27,541 --> 01:17:28,514
Careful, Mike.

1349
01:17:28,619 --> 01:17:30,149
Do you know what he's talking about?

1350
01:17:30,253 --> 01:17:31,607
It's important, sir.

1351
01:17:31,712 --> 01:17:34,875
You come in here and speak to me, I'll kill you.

1352
01:17:34,980 --> 01:17:37,100
Now you're just being idiotic.

1353
01:17:37,204 --> 01:17:39,463
[dishes crash]

1354
01:17:39,567 --> 01:17:42,105
Don't you ever speak to me like that again.

1355
01:17:45,233 --> 01:17:45,928
I'm sorry.

1356
01:17:46,032 --> 01:17:49,369
You know I didn't mean it.

1357
01:17:49,474 --> 01:17:50,724
No!

1358
01:17:50,829 --> 01:17:51,663
No!

1359
01:17:59,275 --> 01:18:02,299
Michael, go.

1360
01:18:02,403 --> 01:18:03,515
Go now.

1361
01:18:20,719 --> 01:18:23,153
It's OK.

1362
01:18:23,257 --> 01:18:25,308
All over now.

1363
01:18:25,412 --> 01:18:26,558
We can all be friends, yes?

1364
01:18:30,069 --> 01:18:33,476
See, now that the sum has gone, I can know

1365
01:18:33,579 --> 01:18:37,889
that I'm amongst my friends.

1366
01:18:37,993 --> 01:18:44,007
So a toast to my friends and my beautiful wife.

1367
01:19:00,447 --> 01:19:03,262
So what do you think?

1368
01:19:03,367 --> 01:19:04,201
I know.

1369
01:19:04,305 --> 01:19:07,189
I feel it too.

1370
01:19:07,295 --> 01:19:10,805
I'm almost sorry I started this.

1371
01:19:10,909 --> 01:19:12,230
Too late now.

1372
01:19:12,334 --> 01:19:14,384
It's up and running.

1373
01:19:14,489 --> 01:19:16,609
It's beyond my control.

1374
01:19:31,867 --> 01:19:33,362
Tell me about you and Michael Cass.

1375
01:19:33,467 --> 01:19:34,161
Tell you what?

1376
01:19:34,265 --> 01:19:36,698
Tell me everything.

1377
01:19:36,803 --> 01:19:38,193
There's nothing to tell.

1378
01:19:38,298 --> 01:19:39,131
I don't believe you.

1379
01:19:39,236 --> 01:19:40,555
I've seen him look at you.

1380
01:19:40,661 --> 01:19:41,738
So?

1381
01:19:41,842 --> 01:19:43,998
He knows nothing could ever happen between us

1382
01:19:44,102 --> 01:19:45,596
because I belong to you.

1383
01:19:49,454 --> 01:19:50,323
Who else?

1384
01:19:50,428 --> 01:19:51,297
Who else what?

1385
01:19:51,401 --> 01:19:52,270
What would you mean?

1386
01:19:52,374 --> 01:19:54,563
Who else had you?

1387
01:19:54,667 --> 01:19:57,483
Now, that is not fair.

1388
01:19:57,587 --> 01:19:58,282
I won't answer that.

1389
01:19:58,388 --> 01:19:59,430
You don't want to know.

1390
01:19:59,534 --> 01:20:02,800
You tell me what I want to know.

1391
01:20:02,905 --> 01:20:03,773
Who else?

1392
01:20:06,902 --> 01:20:08,883
Nobody.

1393
01:20:08,987 --> 01:20:10,065
Nobody.

1394
01:20:10,170 --> 01:20:14,445
Ever since I met you, there has only been you.

1395
01:20:14,548 --> 01:20:18,407
Oh, John, what's the matter with you?

1396
01:20:18,511 --> 01:20:19,380
You tell me.

1397
01:20:19,485 --> 01:20:21,466
You tell me what's happening to me.

1398
01:20:21,569 --> 01:20:23,413
John, you're scaring me.

1399
01:20:23,516 --> 01:20:24,871
You are supposed to be the strong one.

1400
01:20:24,976 --> 01:20:26,053
You're supposed to take care of me.

1401
01:20:26,158 --> 01:20:27,409
Oh, yeah.

1402
01:20:27,513 --> 01:20:28,625
We'll let a fella take care of her, shall we.

1403
01:20:28,730 --> 01:20:31,058
We'll let a fella take care of her.

1404
01:20:31,162 --> 01:20:32,657
Because she's the one who's out of control.

1405
01:20:32,761 --> 01:20:33,734
Because she's floating away.

1406
01:20:33,839 --> 01:20:35,542
Well hold her down.

1407
01:20:35,646 --> 01:20:37,140
Daddy's little problem girl.

1408
01:20:37,245 --> 01:20:39,122
We'll just palm her off onto the black man

1409
01:20:39,226 --> 01:20:42,424
because no one else will have her, because everybody

1410
01:20:42,527 --> 01:20:43,814
knows she's damaged goods.

1411
01:20:43,918 --> 01:20:45,031
That is not true.

1412
01:20:45,135 --> 01:20:47,950
Someone's been telling you lies, John.

1413
01:20:48,054 --> 01:20:51,322
Yeah, someone's been tell me lies.

1414
01:20:51,426 --> 01:20:53,338
You've been telling me lies.

1415
01:20:53,442 --> 01:20:55,944
Now i just want the truth.

1416
01:20:56,049 --> 01:20:57,890
Tell me the truth, bitch.

1417
01:20:57,994 --> 01:21:00,358
Never speak to me like that.

1418
01:21:00,463 --> 01:21:02,513
I don't know you when you could speak to me like that.

1419
01:21:02,617 --> 01:21:05,571
You frighten me.

1420
01:21:05,675 --> 01:21:08,109
I don't want to be with you anymore.

1421
01:21:08,213 --> 01:21:08,874
Hey.

1422
01:21:08,978 --> 01:21:10,820
Where are you going?

1423
01:21:10,925 --> 01:21:11,863
Are you going to him?

1424
01:21:15,096 --> 01:21:17,876
I'm going to Lulu's.

1425
01:21:17,980 --> 01:21:21,038
You listen, you've got this all wrong.

1426
01:21:21,144 --> 01:21:22,012
Ask Lulu.

1427
01:21:22,116 --> 01:21:23,124
Ask Ben.

1428
01:21:23,229 --> 01:21:25,140
Nobody ever loved anybody like I love you.

1429
01:21:25,245 --> 01:21:29,797
But I can't bear to be with you when you're like this.

1430
01:21:29,902 --> 01:21:31,849
Please just let me go.

1431
01:21:31,953 --> 01:22:21,029
Just let me go;

1432
01:22:21,133 --> 01:22:22,767
[whisperings]

1433
01:22:44,491 --> 01:22:46,472
[growling]

1434
01:22:54,709 --> 01:22:57,976
I don't think you should go back there, not tonight anyway.

1435
01:22:58,080 --> 01:23:00,583
Oh, he'll be all right.

1436
01:23:00,687 --> 01:23:03,294
He was never like this before, you know.

1437
01:23:03,398 --> 01:23:07,082
He's just got this thing in his head about Michael.

1438
01:23:07,186 --> 01:23:10,280
Listen, Dessie, this is serious.

1439
01:23:10,385 --> 01:23:12,678
Do you want to know what I think?

1440
01:23:12,782 --> 01:23:14,277
I think he needs help.

1441
01:23:14,381 --> 01:23:15,216
And you need protection.

1442
01:23:15,320 --> 01:23:16,363
Oh, come on, Lulu.

1443
01:23:16,467 --> 01:23:17,683
Well, what do you think, Ben?

1444
01:23:17,787 --> 01:23:18,864
You known him best?

1445
01:23:18,970 --> 01:23:19,907
Don't say that.

1446
01:23:20,012 --> 01:23:23,419
Nobody knows him better than me.

1447
01:23:23,522 --> 01:23:24,496
I love him and he loves me.

1448
01:23:24,599 --> 01:23:25,608
This is just a--

1449
01:23:28,423 --> 01:23:30,230
he needs me.

1450
01:23:30,335 --> 01:23:31,586
He needs me.

1451
01:23:31,690 --> 01:23:35,201
But at least listen to what Ben's got to say, Dessie.

1452
01:23:35,305 --> 01:23:38,259
I think Dessie's right.

1453
01:23:38,364 --> 01:23:39,476
I think John needs you now.

1454
01:23:44,099 --> 01:23:44,932
Maybe more than ever.

1455
01:24:03,041 --> 01:24:05,613
[thunder cracks]

1456
01:24:11,383 --> 01:24:12,252
Ah!

1457
01:24:12,356 --> 01:24:14,928
[car alarm sounds]

1458
01:24:19,655 --> 01:24:22,853
You're wrong about Dessie and me.

1459
01:24:22,957 --> 01:24:24,729
Don't lie to me.

1460
01:24:24,833 --> 01:24:27,718
[sounds of a fight]

1461
01:24:30,777 --> 01:24:31,994
Oh!

1462
01:24:32,098 --> 01:24:33,315
That's enough!

1463
01:24:33,419 --> 01:24:34,358
That's enough.

1464
01:24:34,462 --> 01:24:36,060
I don't want to fight with you.

1465
01:24:44,124 --> 01:24:44,818
[roaring]

1466
01:24:44,923 --> 01:24:48,121
[punching]

1467
01:25:06,785 --> 01:25:08,975
Steven Jackson, former Transport Minister

1468
01:25:09,079 --> 01:25:11,409
and former candidate for the Mayor of London,

1469
01:25:11,512 --> 01:25:14,259
and lastly, Commissioner John Othello

1470
01:25:14,363 --> 01:25:15,543
of the Metropolitan Police.

1471
01:25:15,648 --> 01:25:18,741
But first, let's have a question from Mrs.

1472
01:25:18,846 --> 01:25:21,001
Elena Barrett of Harrad.

1473
01:25:21,105 --> 01:25:24,894
Do the panel believe we live in a racist society,

1474
01:25:24,998 --> 01:25:27,258
and if so, what can we do about it?

1475
01:25:28,370 --> 01:25:29,690
Commissioner John Othello.

1476
01:25:32,644 --> 01:25:33,547
Commissioner?

1477
01:25:38,101 --> 01:25:41,611
You're asking me, do we live in a racist society.

1478
01:25:44,983 --> 01:25:48,146
Yes, obviously.

1479
01:25:48,250 --> 01:25:50,127
So what can we do about it?

1480
01:25:54,645 --> 01:25:56,765
I say, enjoy the advantages it gives you.

1481
01:25:59,442 --> 01:26:02,432
I think we expecting rather more than that, John.

1482
01:26:08,166 --> 01:26:09,035
Commissioner?

1483
01:26:09,140 --> 01:26:11,746
[whisperings]

1484
01:26:51,821 --> 01:26:54,254
Ah.

1485
01:26:54,359 --> 01:26:57,243
It doesn't have to be so bad, John.

1486
01:26:57,347 --> 01:26:59,919
Another day it's someone else.

1487
01:27:00,024 --> 01:27:01,587
What does it matter in the big picture?

1488
01:27:05,132 --> 01:27:07,739
Did you hear about Mike Cass by the way?

1489
01:27:07,844 --> 01:27:10,242
Someone gave him a hiding.

1490
01:27:10,346 --> 01:27:12,536
I reckon he was asking for it, don't you?

1491
01:27:12,640 --> 01:27:14,899
Was he badly hurt?

1492
01:27:15,004 --> 01:27:16,047
He'll live.

1493
01:27:19,488 --> 01:27:24,111
He never saw the guy who hit him, apparently.

1494
01:27:24,215 --> 01:27:26,960
Just one of those things.

1495
01:27:27,065 --> 01:27:28,350
Yesterday's news.

1496
01:27:28,455 --> 01:27:31,027
Yes.

1497
01:27:31,131 --> 01:27:32,000
Yesterday's news.

1498
01:27:32,104 --> 01:27:33,113
That's it.

1499
01:27:33,217 --> 01:27:34,606
Have to get these things in perspective.

1500
01:27:34,711 --> 01:27:36,310
And it's the same with the personal thing.

1501
01:27:36,414 --> 01:27:41,592
You have to see life as a whole, love, sexual love,

1502
01:27:41,697 --> 01:27:45,833
love for a woman, just a tiny part of a man's life.

1503
01:27:45,938 --> 01:27:46,806
Not for me.

1504
01:27:49,934 --> 01:27:52,298
Do you think you're the first man to pick the wrong woman?

1505
01:27:52,403 --> 01:27:54,800
I didn't pick her.

1506
01:27:54,905 --> 01:27:58,554
I just thought I did.

1507
01:27:58,658 --> 01:28:02,759
Thought it was I fell in love with her.

1508
01:28:02,865 --> 01:28:04,845
And what is she now?

1509
01:28:04,949 --> 01:28:07,660
Well, she's your wife, John.

1510
01:28:07,764 --> 01:28:10,198
For better or for worse.

1511
01:28:14,821 --> 01:28:19,652
I got a report back from the bath lab today, John.

1512
01:28:19,756 --> 01:28:32,651
A, B, and C. I'm so sorry.

1513
01:29:31,043 --> 01:29:33,614
[phone rings]

1514
01:29:59,335 --> 01:30:00,204
John.

1515
01:30:00,308 --> 01:30:02,706
I know, Dessie.

1516
01:30:02,810 --> 01:30:05,105
I know.

1517
01:30:05,209 --> 01:30:05,869
What?

1518
01:30:05,973 --> 01:30:07,434
What do you know?

1519
01:30:07,537 --> 01:30:12,125
About you and Cass in my house, in my bed, in my room.

1520
01:30:12,230 --> 01:30:15,323
John, it isn't true.

1521
01:30:15,428 --> 01:30:18,486
Don't lie to me, Dessie.

1522
01:30:18,589 --> 01:30:20,815
I've just told you.

1523
01:30:20,919 --> 01:30:21,579
I know.

1524
01:30:21,683 --> 01:30:23,179
You don't know anything.

1525
01:30:23,283 --> 01:30:25,680
You know nothing about me if you can say something like that.

1526
01:30:25,784 --> 01:30:27,071
No, I don't know anything about you.

1527
01:30:27,175 --> 01:30:28,983
But I do know that I loved you too much

1528
01:30:29,087 --> 01:30:32,597
and I wish I'd never set my eyes on you.

1529
01:30:32,701 --> 01:30:35,135
Because all the time you were somewhere else

1530
01:30:35,239 --> 01:30:39,202
you were with someone else, even in your dreams.

1531
01:30:39,306 --> 01:30:41,843
You were never mine.

1532
01:30:41,947 --> 01:30:45,144
You were never mine.

1533
01:30:45,249 --> 01:30:46,465
I thought you were mine.

1534
01:30:46,569 --> 01:30:48,099
This is just--

1535
01:30:48,204 --> 01:30:49,246
this is madness.

1536
01:30:49,351 --> 01:30:50,775
None of this is true.

1537
01:30:50,879 --> 01:30:52,756
I was always yours, always.

1538
01:30:52,861 --> 01:30:53,938
No.

1539
01:30:54,042 --> 01:30:56,093
No more lies, Dessie, no more lies.

1540
01:30:56,197 --> 01:30:57,449
No more lies.

1541
01:31:01,446 --> 01:31:02,836
I don't like this game anymore.

1542
01:31:02,940 --> 01:31:03,844
You're frightening me.

1543
01:31:03,948 --> 01:31:04,887
This is not a game.

1544
01:31:04,991 --> 01:31:06,346
Not a game.

1545
01:31:06,451 --> 01:31:07,494
A game?

1546
01:31:07,597 --> 01:31:09,440
My life was just a game.

1547
01:31:09,544 --> 01:31:10,656
It was a game-- [scream]

1548
01:31:10,760 --> 01:31:12,082
--to you!

1549
01:31:12,186 --> 01:31:12,950
Wasn't it?

1550
01:31:13,055 --> 01:31:14,340
You're hurting me. John!

1551
01:31:14,446 --> 01:31:15,314
Shh.

1552
01:31:15,418 --> 01:31:16,357
John!

1553
01:31:16,461 --> 01:31:17,295
John!

1554
01:31:17,400 --> 01:31:19,485
Shh!

1555
01:31:19,588 --> 01:31:22,161
[screams]

1556
01:31:28,348 --> 01:31:31,510
[music plays]

1557
01:32:16,834 --> 01:32:17,772
Dessie!

1558
01:32:17,876 --> 01:32:20,240
[door buzzer]

1559
01:32:20,344 --> 01:32:21,213
Dessie.

1560
01:32:21,317 --> 01:32:22,221
It's Lulu.

1561
01:32:22,326 --> 01:32:23,610
Please answer the door.

1562
01:32:23,715 --> 01:32:26,253
Dessie, are you there?

1563
01:32:26,357 --> 01:32:27,226
John!

1564
01:32:38,175 --> 01:32:40,537
Ben, Ben, it's Lulu.

1565
01:32:40,642 --> 01:32:42,415
Please can you come round now?

1566
01:32:42,519 --> 01:32:45,056
[door buzzer]

1567
01:32:45,161 --> 01:32:46,030
[choking moan]

1568
01:32:46,134 --> 01:32:48,045
Dessie!

1569
01:32:48,150 --> 01:32:49,471
Dessie, are you there?

1570
01:32:49,574 --> 01:32:51,243
Please answer the door!

1571
01:32:51,348 --> 01:32:53,536
Dessie!

1572
01:32:53,641 --> 01:32:54,892
Dessie!

1573
01:32:54,996 --> 01:32:58,368
John, John, please, will you answer me?It's Lulu.

1574
01:33:07,162 --> 01:33:10,151
Dessie, please.

1575
01:33:10,255 --> 01:33:12,202
Dessie.

1576
01:33:12,306 --> 01:33:14,287
[glass crashes]

1577
01:33:18,666 --> 01:33:19,534
Oh.

1578
01:33:24,088 --> 01:33:25,027
Oh, god, there's no pulse.

1579
01:33:25,131 --> 01:33:25,999
Get an ambulance.

1580
01:33:26,104 --> 01:33:28,155
No.

1581
01:33:28,259 --> 01:33:31,387
(GROWLING) No ambulance.

1582
01:33:31,492 --> 01:33:32,951
It's over.

1583
01:33:33,056 --> 01:33:36,044
What have you done, John?

1584
01:33:36,149 --> 01:33:36,983
What have you done?

1585
01:33:42,822 --> 01:33:43,969
Look at her.

1586
01:33:44,073 --> 01:33:47,792
She's so sweet.

1587
01:33:47,896 --> 01:33:50,573
Who could guess what a whore she was?

1588
01:33:50,677 --> 01:33:51,998
A whore?

1589
01:33:52,103 --> 01:33:53,354
Who said she was a whore?

1590
01:33:53,458 --> 01:33:55,022
Everybody knows it. You know it.

1591
01:33:55,127 --> 01:33:56,134
Don't like to me.

1592
01:33:56,238 --> 01:33:57,628
She loved you.

1593
01:33:57,732 --> 01:34:02,008
Who told you lies about her? ?

1594
01:34:02,112 --> 01:34:09,411
Who

1595
01:34:09,515 --> 01:34:11,045
Oh, Christ, John.

1596
01:34:14,138 --> 01:34:17,475
I was too late.

1597
01:34:17,579 --> 01:34:19,005
I came as quick as I could.

1598
01:34:19,109 --> 01:34:21,611
I couldn't use the phone, something like this.

1599
01:34:24,149 --> 01:34:31,725
The cops up at the lab, the DNA, it was just A

1600
01:34:31,830 --> 01:34:38,746
and B. She's innocent, John.

1601
01:34:41,735 --> 01:34:42,569
She's clean.

1602
01:34:45,420 --> 01:34:47,957
[moaning cries]

1603
01:34:54,665 --> 01:34:56,611
[sobbing]

1604
01:34:59,774 --> 01:35:02,624
No!

1605
01:35:02,728 --> 01:35:04,674
Ah!

1606
01:35:04,778 --> 01:35:06,100
God!

1607
01:35:06,205 --> 01:35:09,298
Oh, God!

1608
01:35:09,402 --> 01:35:11,035
Oh!

1609
01:35:11,140 --> 01:35:12,426
I'm so sorry.

1610
01:35:12,529 --> 01:35:13,538
It was you.

1611
01:35:16,700 --> 01:35:18,507
Wait outside.

1612
01:35:18,612 --> 01:35:19,482
You can do nothing here.

1613
01:35:19,586 --> 01:35:21,601
He's like a wild animal.

1614
01:35:21,705 --> 01:35:22,610
Anything could happen.

1615
01:35:22,714 --> 01:35:24,035
It was you.

1616
01:35:24,139 --> 01:35:25,632
Get out.

1617
01:35:25,738 --> 01:35:26,606
Get out!

1618
01:35:33,557 --> 01:35:34,427
Steady, John.

1619
01:35:34,530 --> 01:35:36,374
I trusted you.

1620
01:35:36,478 --> 01:35:37,659
John, you've got it all wrong.

1621
01:35:37,763 --> 01:35:39,328
Shut up, Ben.

1622
01:35:39,432 --> 01:35:41,830
Don't lie.

1623
01:35:41,934 --> 01:35:43,465
I can smell it on you.

1624
01:35:43,568 --> 01:35:44,819
You stink of it.

1625
01:35:47,773 --> 01:35:48,990
You did this to me.

1626
01:35:52,848 --> 01:35:55,698
Why?

1627
01:35:55,802 --> 01:35:57,644
Because you took what was mine.

1628
01:36:07,933 --> 01:36:09,879
I never meant to end like this, John.

1629
01:36:14,224 --> 01:36:18,707
I trusted and I loved you.

1630
01:36:18,811 --> 01:36:21,939
I loved you.

1631
01:36:22,044 --> 01:36:22,878
I still do.

1632
01:36:25,519 --> 01:36:26,562
I always will.

1633
01:36:58,816 --> 01:36:59,686
John.

1634
01:37:06,464 --> 01:37:08,618
I don't want you here.

1635
01:37:14,180 --> 01:37:21,097
I have to make things tidy before anybody else comes.

1636
01:37:21,201 --> 01:37:23,182
Go on.

1637
01:37:23,286 --> 01:37:24,225
Get out.

1638
01:37:39,344 --> 01:37:42,368
[sobbing]

1639
01:38:20,948 --> 01:38:25,049
He needs a little more time alone with her.

1640
01:38:25,153 --> 01:38:27,308
I tried to tell him, you know.

1641
01:38:27,413 --> 01:38:29,220
He had nothing to worry about with Dessie.

1642
01:38:32,869 --> 01:38:36,485
It's tragic.

1643
01:38:36,588 --> 01:38:39,160
[music playing]

1644
01:40:02,229 --> 01:40:04,836
[sirens]

1645
01:40:10,710 --> 01:40:11,891
Absolute bloody shame.

1646
01:40:11,996 --> 01:40:13,144
What do you think it could have been?

1647
01:40:13,248 --> 01:40:15,680
Just all too much too soon or what?

1648
01:40:15,784 --> 01:40:17,279
Woman trouble, I gather.

1649
01:40:17,384 --> 01:40:21,276
The wife, a rich man's daughter, bit of a handful.

1650
01:40:21,380 --> 01:40:23,188
Well, it was a brave experiment, wasn't it?

1651
01:40:23,293 --> 01:40:24,578
No one could say we didn't try.

1652
01:40:24,682 --> 01:40:26,247
Nor could it be counted as a failure.

1653
01:40:26,351 --> 01:40:28,784
He did some bloody good things in a short time.

1654
01:40:28,888 --> 01:40:30,730
Better get a safe pair of hands next time.

1655
01:40:42,061 --> 01:40:43,833
[camera snap]

1656
01:40:43,937 --> 01:40:45,919
BEN JAGO: It was about love.

1657
01:40:46,023 --> 01:40:50,229
That's what you've got to understand.

1658
01:40:50,334 --> 01:40:52,592
Don't talk to me about race.

1659
01:40:52,696 --> 01:40:53,913
Don't talk to me about politics.

1660
01:40:57,076 --> 01:41:01,317
It was love, simple as that.

